{"id":"trend_similarity","title":"EchoTime trend similarity","family":"native","definition":"echotime","intro_en":"The trend component smooths each standardized input with the package's Savitzky-Golay settings. It compares both the smoothed levels and their standardized first differences, then combines clipped correlations geometrically. The animation reveals the fitted trend before comparison. This separates the declared smoothing scale from a claim that the observed signal has one uniquely identifiable trend.","intro_zh":"趋势分项按软件的 Savitzky-Golay 设置平滑各标准化输入，分别比较平滑后的水平值和标准化一阶差分，再对截断相关取几何平均。动画先展示拟合趋势，再比较两侧；所声明的平滑尺度不意味着信号存在唯一可识别的趋势。","steps_en":["Apply the declared Savitzky-Golay smoother to both standardized inputs.","Measure correlation between the smooth level curves.","Measure correlation between standardized first differences of those curves.","Clip both correlations and take their geometric mean."],"steps_zh":["按所声明参数对两侧标准化输入进行 Savitzky-Golay 平滑。","比较平滑水平曲线的相关。","比较平滑曲线标准化一阶差分的相关。","截断两个相关并取几何平均。"],"formula":"sqrt(max(corr(T(x),T(y)),0)*max(corr(z(diff(T(x))),z(diff(T(y)))),0))","caveats_en":["The window is length-dependent, so changing n_points changes the smoothing scale.","Smoothing can conceal short events that still matter for the application.","Endpoint interpolation is part of the displayed Savitzky-Golay convention."],"caveats_zh":["窗口随长度变化，改变 n_points 会改变平滑尺度。","平滑可能掩盖应用中重要的短暂事件。","端点插值属于此 Savitzky-Golay 实现约定。"],"sources":[{"label":"EchoTime comparison implementation","url":"https://github.com/ZipengWu365/EchoTime/blob/main/src/echotime/similarity.py"},{"label":"SciPy: Savitzky-Golay filter","url":"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.signal.savgol_filter.html"}],"x":[0.0,0.3,0.9,1.8,2.7,2.1,1.5,1.1,1.3,2.0,2.8,3.4,3.0,2.4,2.1,2.5,3.4,4.2,4.4,4.0,3.7,3.9,4.8,5.2],"y":[1.5,2.0519225760215023,2.5029737413368567,2.8847890070498634,3.3269392741386694,2.933060886050363,2.8090394772296827,2.72585888185695,2.7447210175121164,2.93986243717